  stem:"Consider the following Flask and HTML implementations.\nFlask file: `main.py`\n\n```\nfrom flask import Flask, render_template\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route(\"/text/size/<int:size>/<color>\")\ndef set_size(size, color):\n    style = {\"font-size\": str(size) + \"px\", \"color\": color}\n    return render_template(\"index.html\", css_style=style)\n\napp.run(debug=True)\n\n\n```\n\nHTML file: `index.html`\n\n```\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n    <div style=\"color: {{css_style['color']}}; font-size:{{css_style['font-size']}};\">\n        IITM BS Degree Program\n    </div>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\nAssume that the Flask code is running on the server http://127.0.0.1:5000 without any errors. Choose the correct URL to render the output below.\n\n[Image Description: Rendered text \"IITM BS Degree Program\" displayed in red font color at approximately 20px font size.]",figureNote:"Rendered text \"IITM BS Degree Program\" displayed in red font color at approximately 20px font size.",options:["http://127.0.0.1:5000?text=red&size=20", "http://127.0.0.1:5000?size=20&text=red", "http://127.0.0.1:5000/text/size/red/20", "http://127.0.0.1:5000/text/size/20/red"],key:"D",
