  stem:"Consider the following HTML and Python Flask code.\nFilename: `app.py`\n\n```\nfrom flask import Flask, render_template\napp=Flask(__name__)\n\n@app.route(\"/\")\ndef home():\n    return render_template(\"index.html\")\n\napp.run(debug=True)\n\n\n```\n\nFilename: `index.html`\n\n```\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<body>\n    <div>\n        Output is:\n        {% for i in [1,2,3] %}\n            {% set x = i %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ x }}\n    </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\nAssume that the Flask app is running at http://127.0.0.1:5000. What will be the rendered output in the browser for the URL: http://127.0.0.1:5000?",options:["Output is: 3", "Output is:", "Output is: 1 2 3", "Output is: 1 2 3 3"],key:"B",
